WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:12.144
[Gentle music]
This is F# in VS Code with SharpLsp. Hover any symbol, and the F# compiler tells you exactly what it is: the parser, the basket picker, the pricing.

00:16.350 --> 00:25.691
Completion knows your types. Type List dot for every list function, and narrow it down to minBy. Inside the lambda, the record's fields are right there.

00:39.717 --> 00:44.265
Press F12 on a type to jump to its definition, even in another file.

00:47.683 --> 00:53.733
Shift F12 finds every reference across the project, including code you haven't saved yet.

00:58.950 --> 01:06.836
Quick fixes write code for you. This match misses a case. Press Command dot, and SharpLsp generates the missing case.

01:11.783 --> 01:20.780
Rename a function with F2, and SharpLsp renames it across the whole project. Program.fs already calls it by its new name.

01:33.050 --> 01:42.966
And to try an idea, send code to F# Interactive and run it on the spot. That's F# in SharpLsp. First class, free, and open source.
